  <h2 id="money-check">Money check before you pay</h2>

  <p>Our strongest suggestion: spend about a tenth of your family's education budget on a coding course and exam, and treat anything above a fifth as a warning that needs proof from that exact course. Free and low-priced online lessons do not need this care, so try them first.</p>
  <p>An illustration, not a real fee: if the whole budget is Rs 2 lakh, a tenth is Rs 20,000 and a fifth is Rs 40,000. The rest stays for exam attempts, code books, practice charts and a reserve while you switch.</p>

  <ul class="check-list">
    {courseChecks.map((item) => (<li>{item}</li>))}
  </ul>

  <p>General information, not financial advice; do not borrow for a course, and get fees and refund terms in writing.</p>

  <p>
    A coding job is a first step. The skills you add to it, from audit to clear writing, decide how early you gain financial freedom.
  </p>

